## User preferences

- The user asked “分别给我创建好相关的车道，然后我再 cd 进去使用 claude 启动” -> create or reuse the lanes and hand off copyable `cd` + Claude commands; clearly state actions not executed. [Task 1]
- The user asked to start only after “一切配套东西确认后” -> before handoff independently verify path, branch, HEAD, clean state, dependencies, startup cwd, readable goal card, and distinguish READY_NOW, WAIT_CHECKPOINT, and prohibited starts. [Task 1]
- When parallel agents explore, independently cross-check lane state, dependency gates, and runtime prerequisites rather than relying on one agent report. [Task 1]

## Reusable knowledge

- The verified new lane was `card/w4-safety-r2` at `/Users/Heishing/Desktop/canvas/canvas-learning-system/.claude/worktrees/card-w4-safety-r2`, branch `card/w4-safety-r2`, start `2cacbb0c1103309a8e4f7816e2810a7c52a5fc5c`, clean. The exact `git worktree add -b` command is in the cited rollout. [Task 1]
- At that audit time, legal Wave A was V2, V6, W4-①, W6, W7. W4-② shares the W4 tree and must wait for W4-① completion, independent B/H=0 review, commit, clean state, closed old session, and no active Claude/background agent/Codex/mutating process. W6's final runner gate also waits for the whole W4 lane. [Task 1]
- Do not pre-create `batch9-integration`, W8, or W9. They require W4+V5 revalidation, actual user merge authorization, and a real exact 40-hex `W4_V5_CHECKPOINT`. The old W9 round-9 result `0B/3H/7M/1L` conflicts with round-8 text `3H/4M/2L`; refresh W9 goal/card/SHA/snapshot list before Wave B. [Task 1]
- W9 snapshot safety needs a parent shell with `set -euo pipefail`, explicit COPYLIST rejecting empty/absolute/`..`/missing/symlink entries, two status/inventory samples at least 30 seconds apart, copy inventory byte comparison, parent-external `W9_SOURCE_MANIFEST_SHA256`, and post-exit independent recomputation. [Task 1]

## Failures and how to do differently

- A Batch 9 mechanical `PASS` proves the documents/start matrix, not actual task execution or future checkpoint generation. Do not turn it into completion language. [Task 1]
- The old dirty W9 worktree must not be a Claude `--add-dir` source; use only a read-only explicit snapshot and do not expose feature/old W9 to that session. Preserve unrelated dirty/untracked files: no `git clean`, `reset`, or `add -A`. [Task 1]
- `.claude/settings.json` had `hooks: {}` and `pretool-guard.js` only DD-03; CLAUDE.md's DD-12/DD-13/DD-14 claims were not verified runtime blocks. Manually approve high-risk requests and independently recompute state rather than claiming hooks cover them. [Task 1]

